WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
This is a bot stealing a human comedian's joke.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.260
And he said, sorry, I'm not attracted to you.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.620
And I was like, well, whose fault is that?

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.640
This joke has been stolen from comedian Olivia Carter

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.080
by several AI bot Instagram accounts.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.720
An AI bot stole my joke.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.720
One time I asked out my personal trainer

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.180
and he said, sorry, I'm not attracted to you.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.720
And I was like, well, whose fault is that?

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.840
And these AI avatar accounts are reaping massive followings

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.200
that would have otherwise gone to the human comedians that wrote the jokes

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.500
and increasingly depend on Instagram to put their work out there.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.340
The bot account in question has 214,000 followers,

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.260
while Olivia Carter has 117,000.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.180
Comedian George Brettelson's joke was stolen by an AI chatbot with over 300,000 followers

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.620
that appears to be using Instagram to market its OnlyFans page.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.540
AI stole my joke and my outfit.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.160
Mark Zuckerberg, Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos, every single one has said AI's coming.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.260
It's coming for your jobs.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.580
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.080
and your taxes are gonna fund the whole thing.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:07.780
Every single billionaire, Mark Zuckerberg, Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.320
every single one has said AI is coming.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.760
It's coming for your jobs.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.440
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.140
And your taxes are gonna fund the whole thing.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.240
And half the country is like, goddamn.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.120
Fucking Mexicans.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:31.440
The country hears all that and blames immigrants from south of the border instead.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.940
But these AI avatar comedians are only the latest example of the theft of human creativity

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:43.360
by an industry that was built off it. One Microsoft executive even admitted that AI

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.840
represents the quote, largest theft of human labor in human history. Damning admission was

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.180
revealed in court documents in the New York Times's case against OpenAI. They're alleging

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.260
the company used their copyrighted materials in order to train chat GBT.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.980
Nobody asked for AI-generated comedians.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.900
They clearly aren't funny, and they're taking away creative work from the comedians that

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.260
we actually want to see.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:10.300
But instead of giving users the options who opt out of AI content, Instagram is allowing

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.460
it to take over its entire platform.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.100
I don't think we should filter out AI content.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.420
I think we should let you know if content is AI content.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.260
Instagram even nearly rolled out a feature that would have enabled anyone to use your

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:26.700
Instagram photos to generate AI deepfakes. That is, until public backlash was so strong,

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.500
they had no choice but to walk it back. Instagram is all in on the AI gold rush too.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.660
And at its core, these big tech firms are trying to sell us a technology that was built

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.820
on stealing human creativity so they could sell it back to us for profit.
